WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.160 --> 00:00:02.330
- Dua Lipa is sued by the paparazzi,

00:00:02.330 --> 00:00:05.090
because she shared one
of the paparazzi's photos

00:00:05.090 --> 00:00:06.440
of Dua Lipa.

00:00:06.440 --> 00:00:08.160
This sounds ridiculous,

00:00:08.160 --> 00:00:10.780
except for the fact that
Dua Lipa was the one

00:00:10.780 --> 00:00:12.070
who was in the wrong.

00:00:12.070 --> 00:00:13.300
We see this actually a lot,

00:00:13.300 --> 00:00:15.900
where celebrities use a
photo that's taken of them,

00:00:15.900 --> 00:00:18.170
thinking that they own the
intellectual property rights

00:00:18.170 --> 00:00:19.003
related to it.

00:00:19.003 --> 00:00:20.930
I think this happened to Miley
Cyrus and Brittany Spears.

00:00:20.930 --> 00:00:23.590
The thing is it's the photographer
who owns the copyright

00:00:23.590 --> 00:00:24.423
in the photo,

00:00:24.423 --> 00:00:25.920
even if you take a photo of someone else.

00:00:25.920 --> 00:00:28.420
Often the paparazzi have a
right to take these photos.

00:00:28.420 --> 00:00:30.330
You could have two photographers
taking a picture of,

00:00:30.330 --> 00:00:31.163
I don't know, a tree

00:00:31.163 --> 00:00:33.350
and the photos could
look exactly the same.

00:00:33.350 --> 00:00:35.180
They could be taken at
exactly the same time.

00:00:35.180 --> 00:00:37.580
And each of those photographers
owns the copyright

00:00:37.580 --> 00:00:39.160
in their particular photo.

00:00:39.160 --> 00:00:41.990
And if you're taking a picture
of a person on the street,

00:00:41.990 --> 00:00:43.860
it's not the person on the
street that owns that copyright.

00:00:43.860 --> 00:00:45.240
It's the person that took the photo.

00:00:45.240 --> 00:00:47.290
So just because you are
the subject of a photo,

00:00:47.290 --> 00:00:48.620
doesn't mean that you have the copyright

00:00:48.620 --> 00:00:51.670
and the ability to post
that photo on social media

00:00:51.670 --> 00:00:53.710
and Dua Lipa found out the hard way

00:00:53.710 --> 00:00:55.290
that she didn't own the rights.

00:00:55.290 --> 00:00:56.997
So if we see Dua Lipa in court,

00:00:56.997 --> 00:00:58.897
she's probably going to lose this one.

